STATES (every web branch reproduced; each generic leaf state mapped — no hidden DATA section)
  This surface is a NOTIFICATION toast, not a persistent data panel: the web component is `null` in every state
  except "a new, undismissed version exists". Reproducing the web faithfully therefore means the surface is
  withdrawn (EmptyView) for the non-announce states and PRESENTED for the announce state — the same accepted
  disposition as the AiUsageCard off-mode gate (P4 0237: a web `return null` maps to a withdrawn native phase,
  explicitly "NOT a hidden section"). The generic leaf states map as:
    loading  → idle(.awaitingBaseline): the boot probe has not resolved; a version toast is intentionally absent
               until there is something to announce (web hook pre-resolution). Rendering a skeleton toast on every
               launch would be a fabrication the web does not perform.
    empty    → idle(.upToDate): backend matches the boot baseline (web `!newVersionAvailable` → null).
    error    → idle(.pollError): the web hook SWALLOWS poll errors and keeps the banner silent — reproduced as
               withdrawn, never a visible error box (a QueryError toast here would contradict the source).
    dismissed→ idle(.dismissed): deferred for exactly this version (web `dismissedVersion === latestVersion`).
    presented→ the banner body. While presented the P4 leaf freshness axis renders: live (no note), stale (amber
               note + one-shot auto-refresh on the live→stale transition), offline (muted "last known" note).
  Every idle reason is a distinct, unit-tested classification (so the mapping is explicit and verifiable), even
  though all render the same faithful withdrawn surface.

